  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Quinaldic Acid may interact with ATP synthase subunit a through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is reported to target several entities, including 72 kDa type IV collagenase and Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform, which in turn are targets of other compounds. These intermediates are all implicated in the regulation of ATP synthase subunit a, indicating a potential chain of interactions where Quinaldic Acid could influence the activity of this enzyme through different molecular mechanisms. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights the possibility of a complex regulatory network involving ATP synthase subunit a, with Quinaldic Acid potentially acting as a modulator at various points in this pathway.",
